  "query_preview": "..Severe and flash flooding risk will be the main\nfocus today as the strong upper level low approaching srn CA \nthis morning moves inland and then lifts to the NE as the day\nprogresses. PWATs remain elevated across the area, running \n250-280% of normal for late October. Any thunderstorm today, \nespecially N-NE of Tucson, will be capable of severe wind gusts\nof 58 mph or greater (15-18% chance), large hail of 1\" or \ngreater (15-17% chance), a tornado (5-8% chance of one occurring\nwithin 25 miles of a point), and rainfall rates of 1-2\"/hr. SPC\nsevere weather outlook has eastern Pinal/Pima, nrn Cochise, and\nall of Graham and Greenlee counties with Slight Risk. WPC has\nthe area northeast of a Florence-Oracle-Willcox-San Simon line\nwith Slight Risk of flash flooding. Current Flash flood watch \nremains in effect today for Pinal, Graham and Greenlee counties.\nCWA in a Marginal with a Slight from Tucson NE. Once again, \n\nDrier air moves in for Friday, though some lingering showers \npossible near the NM border, which could linger into the weekend\nas well. \n\nTemperatures near normal today, then cooler than normal Friday \ninto this weekend. Latest NBM has a freeze potential at the \nhighest elevations of the White Mountains Sun/Mon morning.",
